    "summaryAr": "About Us At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code",
    "descriptionAr": "About Us At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company. At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a \"normalized\" problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in. Locations: Austin, San Francisco, or NYC About the Role Cloudflare's developer platform lets developers build full-stack applications that run on a global network. Alongside Workers, developers rely on a growing set of data products: D1 for serverless SQLite, Durable Objects for stateful coordination, KV for global key-value storage, R2 for object storage, and Hyperdrive for connecting to existing databases. This role will be leading a new database product from its earliest days. You will define what the product is, who it is for, and why developers should choose it over the databases they already know. Then you will get it to first customers and see it through to general availability. Your mission in this role is to lead the project of building a database designed for agent-driven development workflows, getting both the core tradeoffs and the fine-grained details right. What You'll Do Run customer discovery to find and sharpen the problem the product should solve. Define the product, its target users, and its positioning against established databases. Work with engineering on core design tradeoffs across consistency, latency, scale, durability, and cost to serve. Recruit design partners and run a private beta that produces honest, usable feedback. Set success metrics and use them to decide what to build, change, or cut. Own pricing and packaging, grounded in customer value and unit economics. Drive the product from first prototype through beta, launch, and GA. Make sure it fits naturally with Workers, Wrangler, and Cloudflare's existing data products. Partner cross-functionally with Product Marketing, Developer Relations, Sales, and Customer Support teams. Represent Cloudflare externally at conferences, community events, customer meetings, and developer-focused initiatives. Examples of Desirable Skills, Knowledge, and Experience Proven experience as an EM, PM or founder. You've led teams to ship before and can point to impact. Experience taking a product from 0 to 1. You are comfortable with ambiguity and can turn an open problem into a clear plan. Real experience building on databases. You have modeled data, written queries, and run SQL or NoSQL databases in production. Solid grasp of distributed-systems tradeoffs. You can reason through replication, consistency models, and failure modes with engineers. Comfort with pricing and unit economics for infrastructure. You know what a workload costs to serve and how that shapes a price. Deep empathy for developers and how they choose and adopt new platforms. You understand what it's like to bet your application on a database someone else built. Hands-on ability to write code and use AI and the Internet to learn new things fast. Exceptional communication and collaboration skills. You can translate between engineering domains and align diverse teams on goals. Passion for design details and polish. You raise the bar for sweating the details. External presentation skills. You can walk into a room of developers and build trust and credibility. Compensation Compensation may be adjusted depending on work location. For Seattle/NYC/California based hires - Estimated annual salary of: $172,000 - $215,000 For SF/Bay Area based hires - Estimated annual salary of: $179,000 - $224,000 Equity This role is eligible to participate in Cloudflare’s equity plan. Benefits Cloudflare offers a complete package of benefits and programs to support you and your family.&nbsp; Our benefits programs can help you pay health care expenses, support caregiving, build capital for the future and make life a little easier and fun!&nbsp; The below is a description of our benefits for employees in the United States, and benefits may vary for employees based outside the U.S. Health &amp; Welfare Benefits Medical/Rx Insurance Dental Insurance Vision Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts Commuter Spending Accounts Fertility &amp; Family Forming Benefits On-demand mental health support and Employee Assistance Program Global Travel Medical Insurance Financial Benefits Short and Long Term Disability Insurance Life &amp; Accident Insurance 401(k) Retirement Savings Plan Employee Stock Participation Plan Time Off Flexible paid time off covering vacation and sick leave Leave programs, including parental, pregnancy health, medical, and bereavement leave &nbsp; What Makes Cloudflare Special? We’re not just a highly ambitious, large-scale technology company. We’re a highly ambiti",
