    "summaryAr": "Protect what matters. Primion Technology is a global solution provider and market leader in Converged Security Solutions and Workforce Management . For more than 30 years, we have supported around 5,000 satisfied customers worldwide who rely on our certified solutions every day. From consulting and planning to development, installation, maintenance, and support, a team of over 470 dedicated experts works passionately",
    "descriptionAr": "Protect what matters. Primion Technology is a global solution provider and market leader in Converged Security Solutions and Workforce Management . For more than 30 years, we have supported around 5,000 satisfied customers worldwide who rely on our certified solutions every day. From consulting and planning to development, installation, maintenance, and support, a team of over 470 dedicated experts works passionately to meet the highest standards. PRIMION France is a key growth market within PRIMION's European expansion strategy, focusing on delivering enterprise-grade, software-centric solutions to mid-size and large organizations across French territory. As an Account Executive (m/f/d) , you will acquire new customers and expand PRIMION's presence across enterprise and mid-market organizations. Positioning our integrated software solutions as strategic business enablers, you will guide prospects through the full sales cycle, from lead qualification and solution discovery to contract negotiation and close. If you enjoy building relationships, uncovering opportunities, and turning them into sustainable business growth, then this role could be the perfect fit for you. Ready to make an impact? Join us in France within a remote first working approach and play a key role in accelerating PRIMION's growth across one of our most important European markets. Your Responsibilities New Business Development Identify, target, and develop new enterprise and mid-market accounts across France, with a focus on PRIMION's key verticals (Critical Infrastructure, Healthcare, Manufacturing, Logistics, Public Sector, Financial Services). Build and maintain a healthy, qualified pipeline to consistently achieve and exceed annual revenue targets. Execute structured prospecting activities including outbound outreach, event networking, partner co-selling, and inbound lead follow-up. Solution Selling & Consultative Engagement Conduct detailed discovery conversations to uncover customer pain points around security compliance (NIS2/KRITIS), workforce efficiency, operational risk, and digital transformation. Position PRIMION's integrated software portfolio as a strategic solution rather than a point product, articulating total cost of ownership and business value. Collaborate with Pre-Sales Engineers to design tailored solution architectures and compelling proposals. Sales Cycle Management Own the full end-to-end sales cycle from first contact to signed contract. Manage complex, multi-stakeholder deals involving IT, Security, Operations, Compliance, HR, and C-level decision-makers. Lead commercial negotiations and work with management to structure commercially sound agreements. Maintain accurate CRM hygiene and provide reliable pipeline forecasting. Market & Account Intelligence Develop deep knowledge of the French market landscape, competitive dynamics, and regulatory environment (NIS2, KRITIS, DORA, and relevant French legislation). Identify whitespace opportunities within existing accounts and coordinate with Customer Success for expansion. Represent PRIMION at French industry events, trade fairs, and sector-specific forums. Cross-functional Collaboration Work closely with Pre-Sales, Product, Customer Success, and Marketing teams to ensure seamless customer experiences and aligned go-to-market execution. Provide market feedback to help shape product roadmap priorities and localization requirements for the French market. Key Qualifications Must-Have 5+ years of B2B sales experience, with at least 3 years in software or SaaS/enterprise technology solutions. Strong hunter mentality with the drive to identify opportunities, build pipeline, and win new business. Demonstrated success in closing complex, multi-stakeholder deals with 6-figure+ contract values. Experience selling to enterprise accounts in at least one of PRIMION's target verticals (Critical Infrastructure, Healthcare, Logistics, Manufacturing, Public Sector, or Financial Services). Strong consultative selling skills with the ability to translate technical capabilities into measurable business outcomes. Comfortable navigating complex organizational structures and building relationships at C-level, VP, and Director level. Native or fluent French speaker; professional English proficiency for internal collaboration. Based in France with the ability and willingness to travel extensively across the territory, with a particular focus on Southern France. Nice-to-Have Experience with physical security, access control, video surveillance, or workforce management solutions. Familiarity with NIS2, KRITIS, or similar European cybersecurity/compliance frameworks relevant to critical infrastructure operators. Experience working with channel partners and system integrators as part of a go-to-market model. Exposure to identity management, OT/IT security convergence, or PSIM platforms. Formal sales methodology certification (MEDDIC, Challenger, SPIN Selling, or similar). What We Offer Protect what matters – Powered by People. At Primion, we lead with human responsibility and win through collaboration. Our aim is to build long-term relationships based on mutual respect and trust. That's why we offer you: Impact: Benefit from a high-impact, high-autonomy commercial role with significant territory ownership and the opportunity to directly influence PRIMION's growth across the French market. Compensation: Enjoy a competitive base salary complemented by a capped, performance-based variable compensation structure that rewards success. Stability: Benefit from the backing of an established European technology brand with a 30+ year track record, strong R&D investment, and a clear multi-year growth strategy. Market Opportunity: Capitalize on growing market demand driven by regulatory developments such as NIS2 and KRITIS, creating strong opportunities for customer acquisition and business growth. Collaboration: Work closely with Pre-Sales experts, Customer Success Managers, and Product ",
