    "summaryAr": "Perplexity is seeking a highly motivated Account Executive to lead our growth in the legal industry. You'll drive new business with law firms and corporate legal teams, helping them adopt Perplexity Enterprise to research faster, work from trusted sources and bring AI into high-stakes work securely. This role is ideal for proactive sales professionals who know how legal organizations buy, thrive at the intersection o",
    "descriptionAr": "Perplexity is seeking a highly motivated Account Executive to lead our growth in the legal industry. You'll drive new business with law firms and corporate legal teams, helping them adopt Perplexity Enterprise to research faster, work from trusted sources and bring AI into high-stakes work securely. This role is ideal for proactive sales professionals who know how legal organizations buy, thrive at the intersection of technology and business, and want to shape how AI shows up in the legal profession. Responsibilities Drive new business by prospecting, pitching, and closing Perplexity Enterprise with both leading law firms and in-house legal teams at enterprises Build a vertical point of view: research firms, develop account strategies and run outreach tailored to legal workflows and buying committees Lead the full sales cycle, from first meeting through security and compliance review, procurement, negotiation, close and onboarding Build senior relationships with managing partners, general counsel, CIOs, innovation and knowledge management leaders Run high-impact demos and respond to RFPs, security questionnaires and technical inquiries Partner with Product, Marketing and Customer Success to shape legal use cases, messaging and customer outcomes Bring market feedback from the legal vertical back to Product Meet or exceed individual revenue targets on a monthly and quarterly basis Keep accurate pipeline and account records in Salesforce Qualifications 5+ years of full-cycle SaaS sales experience, with a track record selling into law firms or corporate legal teams Proven record of meeting or exceeding annual revenue targets in a high-growth environment Understanding of how legal organizations evaluate and buy technology, including partner committees, confidentiality and data security requirements Skilled at complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles and tailoring messaging to attorneys, legal ops and IT Proven success self-sourcing pipeline through outbound prospecting Exceptional written and verbal communication, comfortable presenting to senior partners and executives Experience with CRM systems (e.g. Salesforce) Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience Nice to have Experience selling legal tech, legal research, e-discovery or AI products An existing network across law firms or in-house legal teams JD or prior legal industry experience",
