    "summaryAr": "About the Team OpenAI didn’t begin as a traditional company. It began as an idea: that artificial intelligence could be developed in a way that benefits everyone. As a creative team, our role is to help make sure the work behind that idea is understood, as it leaves the lab and meets the world. This company works at the frontier of intelligence. Like any frontier, it’s unfinished, constantly shifting, and still being",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team OpenAI didn’t begin as a traditional company. It began as an idea: that artificial intelligence could be developed in a way that benefits everyone. As a creative team, our role is to help make sure the work behind that idea is understood, as it leaves the lab and meets the world. This company works at the frontier of intelligence. Like any frontier, it’s unfinished, constantly shifting, and still being explored. Our job is to stay close to that uncertainty and help shape how this story gets told, in a way that feels grounded and human. We do this through campaigns, launches, films, brand systems, and work that doesn’t fit neatly into any of those categories yet. This team is for people who want to help shape something from the beginning. About the Role OpenAI’s in-house Creative Team is looking for a Motion Design Producer to help shape and scale how our brand comes to life through motion design across every touchpoint — from identity systems and campaigns to product, web, and comms work. You’ll partner closely with our Brand Identity & Brand Design leadership to manage intake, resourcing, timelines, and creative workflows — ensuring design projects move seamlessly from concept to delivery. You’ll serve as the operational backbone of the design practice, building clarity and momentum across a growing cross-functional team. As Motion Design is a shared function in Creative Design, you will also partner closely with other production functional ecosystems to deliver motion design support. This is a highly collaborative role that requires both strategic oversight and hands-on execution. You’ll be a key connector across Marketing, Product, Comms, and Web — driving alignment, enabling great design, and creating the systems that keep our creative work consistent, efficient, and impactful. In this role, you will: Manage Day-to-day Motion Design Operations: Oversee the end-to-end management of design projects — from scoping and prioritization to delivery — ensuring resources, timelines, and dependencies are well-planned and communicated. Produce High-Priority Motion Projects: Serve as a hands-on individual contributor (IC) on large, high-priority motion projects, owning production from kickoff through delivery. Shape Intake & Resourcing: Partner with creative and marketing, creative, production and ops leads to evaluate new requests, define scope, and allocate design capacity across internal and external partners. Build Cross-Functional Alignment: Act as the connective tissue between design and partner teams (Product, Web, Brand, Comms, and GTM), ensuring design work ladders up to broader strategic goals. Elevate Systems & Process: Design and implement operational frameworks that enable the design team to scale effectively — from creative reviews and feedback loops to asset tracking and tool optimization. Manage External Partners: Oversee relationships with design vendors, freelancers, and production partners; ensure output meets OpenAI’s creative and technical standards. Uphold Craft & Consistency: Partner with the Brand Identity and Brand Design team to ensure design work is cohesive, high-quality, and reflective of OpenAI’s evolving visual identity. You might thrive in this role if you: Have 8+ years of experience in design production, brand operations, or creative program management within an in-house team or agency environment. Are fluent in the design process — from concept and iteration through production and delivery — and can anticipate what a creative team needs to succeed. Should be experienced in full identity explorations and production needs. Are a natural systems-builder who can bring order to complexity without stifling creativity. Excel at stakeholder management and communication — you’re equally comfortable talking to designers, executives, and engineers. Are proactive, unflappable, and skilled at driving clarity in fast-moving environments. Are fluent in tools like Asana, Airtable, Figma, and Google Workspace. Have experience building or scaling global brand systems. Have familiarity with motion, 3D, or experiential design production. Have a strong understanding of creative operations in a technology-driven or design-led organization. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the ",
