    "summaryAr": "The Learning Team at ClickHouse is growing fast as more users discover the power of ClickHouse and seek to understand how to use it effectively. As a Training Operations Specialist, you will be responsible for coordinating, managing, and supporting the logistics and administration of global training programs, with a focus on public and private instructor-led training events. You will collaborate with internal stakeho",
    "descriptionAr": "The Learning Team at ClickHouse is growing fast as more users discover the power of ClickHouse and seek to understand how to use it effectively. As a Training Operations Specialist, you will be responsible for coordinating, managing, and supporting the logistics and administration of global training programs, with a focus on public and private instructor-led training events. You will collaborate with internal stakeholders to ensure seamless event execution and a consistent, high-quality learner experience. What you will be doing: Here is a list of the typical tasks you would be performing as a Training Operations Specialist: Schedule and organize virtual and in-person training events, including registration page setup, Zoom configuration, and email communications. Coordinate training event logistics, including sourcing and booking venues, managing event requirements, coordinating instructor availability, and communicating with instructors and attendees. Manage event registration, monitor enrollment, send reminders, follow-up emails, and track attendance to ensure smooth event execution. Track and report training metrics, registration trends, attendance, and program outcomes to key stakeholders. Partner with Field Marketing teams to coordinate public training events, including event scheduling, registration monitoring, and promotional support. Collaborate with Sales teams to coordinate private training requests, manage scheduling and logistics, and support customer training needs. Work closely with the broader Training team to coordinate resources, streamline processes, and ensure consistent execution across training programs. Requirements: 2+ years of experience in training coordination, operations, event management, or a related role. Proficiency with marketing automation platforms, particularly Marketo, including registration management and email communications. Proficiency with online communication and collaboration tools, including Zoom, Google Workspace, and Notion. Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities across various time zones simultaneously. Detail-oriented, with excellent organizational, time management, communication, and process management skills. Ability to learn new technologies and systems quickly and effectively. A self-motivated attitude with the desire and determination to complete tasks in a fast-paced startup environment. Bonus points: Experience working with Learning Management Systems (LMS). Experience with Salesforce, particularly reporting, dashboards, and tracking training-related data. Background in project management, curriculum design, or learning and development. Experience coordinating instructor-led training programs across multiple regions or global audiences. Perks Flexible work environment - ClickHouse is a globally distributed company and remote-friendly. We currently operate in over 25 countries. Healthcare - Employer contributions towards your healthcare. Equity in the company - Every new eligible team member who joins our company receives equity. Time off - Flexible time off in the US, generous entitlement in other countries. A USD$500 Home office setup if you’re a remote employee. Global Gatherings – We believe in the power of in-person connection and offer opportunities to engage with colleagues at company-wide offsites. Culture - We All Shape It As part of a rapidly scaling start-up, you will be instrumental in shaping our culture. Are you interested in finding out more about our culture? Learn more about our values here . Check out our blog posts or follow us on LinkedIn to find out more about what’s happening at ClickHouse. Equal Opportunity & Privacy ClickHouse provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type based on factors such as race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Please see here for our Privacy Statement.",
