    "summaryAr": "ClickHouse is powering the next generation of real-time analytics and AI infrastructure. We recently raised a $400M Series D at a $15B valuation, and we're growing fast: expanding our customer base, scaling our cloud business, and widening our product line through acquisitions and net-new Tier-1 launches into new product categories. We're looking for a Principal Technical Program Manager, GTM Integration & Launch to ",
    "descriptionAr": "ClickHouse is powering the next generation of real-time analytics and AI infrastructure. We recently raised a $400M Series D at a $15B valuation, and we're growing fast: expanding our customer base, scaling our cloud business, and widening our product line through acquisitions and net-new Tier-1 launches into new product categories. We're looking for a Principal Technical Program Manager, GTM Integration & Launch to own how those products get to market. An acquired product isn't sellable on day one, and neither is a Tier-1 launch: the pricing, packaging, quoting logic, approval rules, and controls have to be built and tested end-to-end, the acquired base has to be migrated onto ClickHouse paper, and the field has to know who to sell it to and how they get paid for it. This role owns getting there. Reporting to the Sr. Director of Global Revenue Operations, you'll own the path to market across Product, Finance, Legal, Operations, Engineering, Enablement, and the acquired team: the commercial diligence, the requirements, the design decisions, the build, the testing, and go-live readiness. You'll also shape the GTM plan itself – who we sell to first, how reps are compensated, how the field is trained – and report monthly to leadership on how our emerging products are actually selling. Beyond any single launch, you'll turn integration into a repeatable playbook and build the tooling that makes the commercial system faster and more reliable. This is a senior individual contributor role on the critical path for every acquisition and every Tier-1 launch. What You'll Be Doing Own the integration path for acquired products. Bring an acquired offering onto the commercial system, reconcile its pricing and contract mechanics with how ClickHouse sells, and get it sellable through the same standard as an organic launch. Shape GTM strategy for the products you're integrating. Help define the motion for newly acquired products (e.g., Langfuse) and net-new Tier-1 launches (e.g., Postgres): who we sell to first and why, how reps get paid for it, and how the field gets trained – partnering with Sales Leadership, Comp/Planning, and Enablement, and building the target account lists from usage signals and account intelligence. Run commercial diligence and pre-close planning. Assess the target's pricing model, contract paper, billing stack, metering, and revenue recognition, and land at close with a sequenced integration plan rather than a blank page. Own the commercial and operational design. Define the requirements and make the calls on pricing setup, quoting logic, discount and approval rules, and the controls that govern how the product gets sold, in partnership with Commercial leadership. Own contract and customer migration. Map the acquired base's entitlements to ClickHouse SKUs, move customers onto ClickHouse paper at renewal, and protect revenue through the transition. Own the program end-to-end. Hold the timeline, drive deliverables across Product, Finance, Legal, Operations, Engineering, and the acquired team, and synthesize the cross-functional work into a single readiness plan. Test the end-to-end flow before launch. Run UAT on the quote-to-cash path, catch what breaks, and confirm the full flow works before go-live. Own go-live readiness. Set the launch criteria with product marketing, run the go/no-go, and make the call on whether the flow is ready. Coordinate field activation with Enablement so the product lands when it ships. Own monthly GTM reporting. Report wins, gaps, and what broke to leadership, and feed it back into the process so the next integration goes faster. Build the playbook and the tooling. Turn each integration into a repeatable path, and find and fix what's manual, slow, or error-prone in the commercial system along the way. What You Bring 10+ years in technical program management, revenue operations, product operations, or commercial systems, with a track record of owning launches end-to-end and building the systems behind them. Direct experience building GTM strategy for a new or unproven product. Experience with usage-based or consumption-based business models. You understand how metering, commits, and overages create dependencies across billing, contracts, revenue recognition, and the commercial system – and that a launch has to get all of them right together. Strong working knowledge of the systems an integration depends on: Salesforce and CPQ, financial and billing systems, product rating, and telemetry. You can design quoting rules, approval logic, and automated controls across them. Depth to own the design, not just the plan. You write the requirements, facilitate the design calls on quoting, approval, and control logic, and build parts of the solution yourself. Sales compensation design experience, or direct partnership with Sales/Comp teams on incentive structures. M&A or technology integration experience. Bringing an acquired product onto the commercial system runs the same path as an organic launch, and this role owns that work. Cross-functional program management at the core. You hold a timeline, drive deliverables across teams, and synthesize across stakeholders. You measure readiness by whether the full flow works end-to-end. Partnership with enablement teams to build training programs and measure them against outcome metrics. Strong analytical skills, including SQL, to build target lists, measure pilot results, and report on launch effectiveness. Strong written and verbal communication. Comfortable driving a cross-functional forum and presenting readiness status to senior stakeholders. Bachelor's degree; quantitative or technical field preferred. MBA or equivalent experience a plus. Perks Flexible work environment - ClickHouse is a globally distributed company and remote-friendly. We currently operate in over 25 countries. Healthcare - Employer contributions towards your healthcare. Equity in the company - Every new eligible team member who joins our company rec",
