    "summaryAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are r",
    "descriptionAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. Co-create the future with us as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software. * Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab. An overview of this role As a Senior Executive Assistant in GitLab’s Marketing organization, you’ll support the Vice President (VP) of Growth Marketing and the VP of Product Marketing, reporting to the VP of Growth Marketing. You’ll help both leaders focus on their highest-impact work across teams spanning digital experience, marketing operations, events, community and developer relations, campaigns, product marketing, and launches. Beyond calendar management, you’ll participate in leadership discussions, keep projects and recurring meetings moving, and connect the leaders with their organizations through a monthly launch rhythm. In your first year, you’ll build trusted relationships with both leaders and their teams and establish reliable processes for scheduling, meeting preparation, travel, events, recruiting coordination, and expenses. You’ll anticipate needs one to two weeks ahead and follow commitments through to completion, moving quickly as priorities shift. What you’ll do Own high-volume calendars across time zones for both leaders, connecting meeting priorities to quarterly goals and business rhythms. Recommend how to prioritize or delegate requests, and provide inbox triage when requested. Prepare leadership meetings, all-hands, and the monthly in-person launch review: coordinate agendas, pre-reads, and attendance, keep time, and capture and follow up on action items. Maintain the leadership project tracker and weekly leadership, monthly goals, and quarterly business reviews. Build work-back plans, follow up with owners, and flag delays, deadlines, and decisions so the right people stay involved and informed. Coordinate domestic and international travel, including transportation, lodging, security needs, and documentation. Arrange alternatives when plans change, and prepare accurate monthly expense reports with receipts and reconciliation. Plan team offsites, leadership working sessions, and company kickoffs from start to finish, working with event partners and confirming reservations, deposits, and logistics through completion. Partner with Recruiting and hiring teams on interviews, candidate communication, and onboarding logistics, and with People, information technology (IT), and Security on team needs. Provide coverage for executive support partners, help onboard new support partners, and take on Marketing special projects. Partner with senior leaders and their teams, helping team leads succeed. Use artificial intelligence (AI) tools, with Claude as our standard, to streamline research, drafting, meeting summaries, and recurring administrative work. Check outputs for accuracy and context rather than relying on automated summaries alone. Build automations and repeatable workflows to handle high-volume work quickly. Identify recurring friction in how the teams work, and propose and implement improvements to processes and documentation. Build warm, proactive relationships across both teams, including timely recognition of milestones and quick, thoughtful gestures such as notes and gifts. What you’ll bring Experience supporting two or more VP-level leaders simultaneously at a fast-paced, AI-forward company, adapting to distinct working styles and business priorities. An organized, reliable approach to balancing priorities, taking ownership within agreed priorities, and communicating progress proactively, moving quickly, and figuring things out independently with limited resources. Experience managing complex calendars across time zones, using judgment to balance competing requests and checking scheduling details and attendees. Project management skills, including building work-back plans, following up with owners, and keeping multiple workstreams moving with minimal oversight. Experience coordinating international travel and team events from start to finish, anticipating dependencies, responding to disruptions, and confirming arrangements through completion. Proficiency with Google Workspace, Slack, Zoom, Okta, Navan, Claude, and GitLab, alongside experience with expense reporting, recruiting coordination, and onboarding logistics. Demonstrated fluency with AI tools and a track record of automating recurring work. Clear, warm, approachable, and proactively personable communication across functions and levels, sound judgment with confidential information, and experience building trusted relationships in a remote, asynchronous environment where documentation and written communication are central. Ability to navigate multi-stakeholder requests with tact, balancing protection of the leaders’ time with support for key teammates. Flexibility to s",
