    "summaryAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are r",
    "descriptionAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. Co-create the future with us as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software. * Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab. Role overview As a Strategic Enterprise Account Executive for ANZ, you will own and grow GitLab’s enterprise relationships across Australia. You’ll help large organizations realize the full value of GitLab’s AI-powered DevSecOps platform through strategic, consultative SaaS sales. You’ll engage customers on how Agentic AI, AI orchestration, and integrated security can support secure software development and business outcomes. You’ll lead the end-to-end sales cycle—from territory and account planning, prospecting, and qualification through complex deal execution, deployment, adoption, and long-term expansion. Reporting to our Regional Sales Director, you’ll take a customer-centric approach to understanding complex business and technical needs, guiding customers through evaluation, and coordinating pre- and post-sales resources to achieve successful deployments and measurable business outcomes. You’ll operate with minimal supervision on complex enterprise opportunities, act as the voice of the customer within GitLab, and partner closely with strategic channel partners to generate qualified pipeline and win new customers. In your first year, you’ll establish and execute account plans for enterprise prospects and customers across ANZ, build trusted relationships with internal and external stakeholders, and manage your pipeline and forecast with transparency and discipline. What you’ll do Support GitLab’s strategic prospects and customers in the ANZ Market, owning the full sales cycle for large and enterprise accounts&nbsp; Lead account strategy by developing and executing account plans aligned to each customer’s business needs and long-term goals Conduct prospecting and opportunity development activities in named large and strategic accounts, including working closely with strategic channel partners to generate qualified leads and new customers Coordinate pre- and post-sales engagement with solutions architects, customer success, and support teams to ensure successful rollout, adoption, and expansion of GitLab products Provide clear account leadership, including regular activity, pipeline, and forecast reporting to sales management Analyze wins and losses, contribute to root cause analysis, and share lessons learned with account managers, marketing, and technical teams to improve future outcomes Act as the voice of the customer by sharing feedback and product ideas through GitLab’s public issue tracker and internal channels Use a consultative sales approach to uncover business issues, shape solution recommendations, and deliver compelling proposals, quotes, and presentations that address customer requirements &nbsp; What you’ll bring Experience managing complex sales cycles with ANZ large, strategic enterprise customers. Proven ability to prospect, qualify, and develop new opportunities while also growing existing accounts through strong account management. Familiarity with software development concepts and tools; exposure to Git, software development tools, DevSecOps, application lifecycle management, Agentic AI, AI orchestration, or software and application security is preferred. Proficiency in consultative, solution, value-based, and consumption-based selling—including discovery, uncovering business needs, aligning solutions to customer outcomes, driving product adoption and expansion, and delivering persuasive proposals and presentations. Skill in leading pre- and post-sales activities, coordinating with technical, support, and channel partners to drive adoption and expansion Proficiency in consultative selling, including uncovering business needs, building account plans, and delivering proposals and presentations that align GitLab solutions to customer outcomes Ability to prepare and maintain accurate activity, pipeline, and forecast reports, and to contribute to win/loss and root cause analysis Effective communication and collaboration skills to share customer feedback and lessons learned with sales management, product, marketing, and technical teams Familiarity with software development concepts and tools, with preferred exposure to Git, software development tools, or application lifecycle management Alignment with GitLab’s values, openness to learning, and interest in applying transferable skills even if your background does not match every requirement exactly About the team The Strategic Account Executive will join our enterprise sales team, which focuses on driving GitLab adoption with large customers in the ANZ market. The team is responsible for the full relationship lifecycle with enterprise accounts, from initial engagement through long-term",
